            <ArticleTitle>[Total occlusion of the left common coronary artery--a case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>919-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Total chronic occlusion of the left main coronary artery is an unusual finding. After a review of the literature, the authors present a case report of a patient with stable angina and total occlusion of the left main coronary artery, right coronary with atherosclerotic lesions and normal ventricular function.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
